## Principles
Use only an existing authorized yihou allocation; revalidate job126175/node055 before use. NEVER use crsuse2-m2m-234 or crsuse2-m2m-036. NEVER submit/request/cancel allocations. Inspect ownership before stopping any task; preserve other users' work and supervisors. Use own Docker container with yihou in its name. Do not delete any file whose name lacks yihou. No host dependency installation or daemon changes. No commits/pushes.

Use iterative-debug-loop; every experiment has an iterations/ directory and working_process.md entry. At least three evidence sources for serious diagnosis, including reference comparison when applicable. Read runtime/speculative/env-var skills before editing those areas. Use LSP/Serena where available, inspect pinned source rather than assume latest APIs. Ask before large core-library changes. English work files, Chinese user reports.

## Team and checks
Leader owns environment, launch and integration. decode-research owns bench implementation and CPU tests. No subagent verification of leader work. Session timers: mission every10min, team checkpoint every20min; log new issues first, intervene on next checkpoint if unresolved. Allow about30min for graph/JIT compilation with progress evidence.
